# Applies to both images: the build context is the repo root for each of them, because `common/` is
# a sibling of the worker directories rather than a subdirectory of either.
#
# Note what is NOT here: neither `transcribe/` nor `coding/` is excluded from the other's build. A
# worker image therefore carries the other's source — a few dozen KB of Python that nothing imports,
# against a base image of many GB. Excluding it would mean two `.dockerignore` files and a build
# that breaks the day a module moves; the trade is not close.
.git
.github
tests
corpus
bench-results.jsonl
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.venv
*.md
